with the name badge and it's...

1202
00:56:32.208 --> 00:56:34.457
and you get Slurpees
thrown at you, and it's,

1203
00:56:34.458 --> 00:56:36.791
it's humbling. It's humbling,
and it was, it was good for me.

1204
00:56:36.792 --> 00:56:40.290
But I want to... I'm sure you're wondering,
where is he going with all this?

1205
00:56:40.291 --> 00:56:42.332
And this is, this is
where I'm going with it.

1206
00:56:42.333 --> 00:56:44.124
For those two years,

1207
00:56:44.125 --> 00:56:47.749
when people asked me
what the doctrine was,

1208
00:56:47.750 --> 00:56:52.290
and they said, "Hey, I am gay,
or I feel, you know,

1209
00:56:52.291 --> 00:56:55.082
"like I'd feel like,
I like girls,

1210
00:56:55.083 --> 00:56:56.290
and what do I do about this?"

1211
00:56:56.291 --> 00:56:58.958
I taught that it was a sin

1212
00:56:58.959 --> 00:57:03.124
because that's what
I had been raised to teach.

1213
00:57:03.125 --> 00:57:06.124
I never felt it in my heart
since I was young.

1214
00:57:06.125 --> 00:57:08.040
I hold regret
about that to this day.

1215
00:57:08.041 --> 00:57:09.791
I wish I could
knock all those doors.

1216
00:57:09.792 --> 00:57:14.040
I wish I could re-knock them,
and tell them that I was wrong.

1217
00:57:14.041 --> 00:57:15.290
I can't do that.

1218
00:57:15.291 --> 00:57:17.749
All I can do is come forward
to you today and tell you,

1219
00:57:17.750 --> 00:57:21.124
I sincerely am sorry.
I, really, in my heart...

1220
00:57:26.583 --> 00:57:28.541
Thank you for this.
This is such a great honor.

1221
00:57:28.542 --> 00:57:31.708
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

1222
00:57:31.709 --> 00:57:35.833
And I know... I know it's been
said, but love is love.

1223
00:57:35.834 --> 00:57:38.499
Love is love.
Thank you so much.

1224
00:57:40.667 --> 00:57:43.749
We're less than two months
out from the LoveLoud Festival,

1225
00:57:43.750 --> 00:57:47.457
which is super intimidating
and scary for a million reasons

1226
00:57:47.458 --> 00:57:50.874
because it feels like we're still
just getting stuff together.

1227
00:57:50.875 --> 00:57:52.541
And just say,
"Take one." Take one.

1228
00:57:52.542 --> 00:57:54.916
I'm here to make
a very special announcement.

1229
00:57:54.917 --> 00:57:58.165
On August 26th,
in the Provo area,

1230
00:57:58.166 --> 00:58:01.290
we're gonna be putting on
a concert called LoveLoud...

1231
00:58:01.291 --> 00:58:05.290
So with LoveLoud, we knew
it was important to be in Utah.

1232
00:58:05.291 --> 00:58:08.749
And I don't want to say
that people were intentionally

1233
00:58:08.750 --> 00:58:10.457
trying to curb this event.

1234
00:58:10.458 --> 00:58:12.541
We can give them
a sponsorship, like a...

1235
00:58:12.542 --> 00:58:13.999
But when we started realizing

1236
00:58:14.000 --> 00:58:16.457
it was a lot of people being
afraid to touch this issue.

1237
00:58:16.458 --> 00:58:19.916
I thought we were
gonna have a massive park.

1238
00:58:19.917 --> 00:58:22.124
We're gonna show that
the whole state of Utah

1239
00:58:22.125 --> 00:58:23.624
actually believes in this.

1240
00:58:23.625 --> 00:58:28.959
The reality hitting me is
that not all of Utah wants this.

1241
00:58:30.083 --> 00:58:31.666
I had tons of people
who were like,

1242
00:58:31.667 --> 00:58:34.666
you shouldn't talk about
how we have, like,

1243
00:58:34.667 --> 00:58:36.374
any issues with suicide.

1244
00:58:36.375 --> 00:58:38.290
Let's not talk about that.

1245
00:58:38.291 --> 00:58:41.499
I'm a little nervous to even click on the
comments section, to be honest with you here.

1246
00:58:41.500 --> 00:58:44.791
"I know many LGBTQ-XYZ people,

1247
00:58:44.792 --> 00:58:47.416
"and while I treat them like
any other person I know,

1248
00:58:47.417 --> 00:58:50.249
I don't agree with their choices
to live that lifestyle."

1249
00:58:50.250 --> 00:58:52.666
People might laugh
because they might say, like,

1250
00:58:52.667 --> 00:58:57.332
why is this straight white guy
the poster child for this now?

1251
00:58:57.333 --> 00:58:59.874
I don't know.
People love to hate, you know?

1252
00:58:59.875 --> 00:59:01.541
So, we'll see what happens.

1253
00:59:01.542 --> 00:59:06.332
"Ditch Your Imagine Dragons Music
because Dan Reynolds Embraced the Poz."

1254
00:59:06.333 --> 00:59:07.624
P-O-Z.

1255
00:59:07.625 --> 00:59:10.624
So I had no idea what that was,
so I googled it.

1256
00:59:10.625 --> 00:59:13.958
"Gay slang, willing to have sex
with someone who is HIV positive

1257
00:59:13.959 --> 00:59:15.375
by someone who is not."

1258
00:59:16.542 --> 00:59:18.082
You start to feel,

1259
00:59:18.083 --> 00:59:22.999
upset that it's, like,
so blatantly obvious.

1260
00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:24.749
Like, look how obvious this is!

1261
00:59:24.750 --> 00:59:27.332
Like, of course we have to love
and accept everybody.

1262
00:59:27.333 --> 00:59:28.791
Come on, guys!

1263
00:59:28.792 --> 00:59:33.082
It's a terrible challenge
to go into this intersection

1264
00:59:33.083 --> 00:59:38.332
of LGBT individuals
and communities of faith,

1265
00:59:38.333 --> 00:59:41.416
which requires sensitivity
on both sides,

1266
00:59:41.417 --> 00:59:42.958
and a lot of nuance,

1267
00:59:42.959 --> 00:59:46.290
and that is not
an easy spot to be

1268
00:59:46.291 --> 00:59:47.999
when you're someone like Dan.

1269
00:59:48.000 --> 00:59:51.374
You know, I just did
an interview with Billboard,

1270
00:59:51.375 --> 00:59:54.791
and my family saw it, and
that's been a little difficult.

1271
00:59:54.792 --> 00:59:57.499
Feeling like the family thinks
that I'm doing something wrong,

1272
00:59:57.500 --> 00:59:59.833
or I'm, like, making them
look like bigots or something.

1273
00:59:59.834 --> 01:00:03.249
That's, that's been, probably,
the hardest thing for me.

1274
01:00:03.250 --> 01:00:07.290
The risk is that in going
to this vulnerable intersection,

1275
01:00:07.291 --> 01:00:09.499
of not just,
I wanna help LGBT individuals

1276
01:00:09.500 --> 01:00:11.332
have more peace and love
and acceptance in their lives,

1277
01:00:11.333 --> 01:00:14.249
but I'm gonna have
an event in Provo, Utah,

1278
01:00:14.250 --> 01:00:17.290
and I'm going to talk
about Mormon doctrine.

1279
01:00:17.291 --> 01:00:20.249
Will you express it in
a way that sounds like

1280
01:00:20.250 --> 01:00:23.249
kicking somebody when they're
down or throwing a stone?

1281
01:00:23.250 --> 01:00:25.708
Or will it come across
as someone that's

1282
01:00:25.709 --> 01:00:28.457
putting his arms around his
fellow brothers and sisters,

1283
01:00:28.458 --> 01:00:31.499
and saying, hey,
let's do better.

1284
01:00:31.500 --> 01:00:33.791
It makes the family nervous.

1285
01:00:33.792 --> 01:00:36.290
But I love Dan and know
he wants to do good.

1286
01:00:36.291 --> 01:00:39.374
I know he's trying to be good,
and I know he means well.

1287
01:01:18.250 --> 01:01:20.374
<i>♪ If I were you ♪</i>

1288
01:01:20.375 --> 01:01:21.791
<i>♪ I'd run away ♪</i>

1289
01:01:21.792 --> 01:01:26.332
<i>♪ Closing your eyes
and count to 10 ♪</i>

1290
01:01:26.333 --> 01:01:28.374
<i>♪ Bird in the sky ♪</i>

1291
01:01:28.375 --> 01:01:30.249
<i>♪ Peace in your mind ♪</i>

1292
01:01:30.250 --> 01:01:31.874
There was a week in particular

1293
01:01:31.875 --> 01:01:36.249
where everything with LoveLoud
was basically falling apart.

1294
01:01:36.250 --> 01:01:39.916
Why is it so much more difficult
than I thought it would be?

1295
01:01:39.917 --> 01:01:43.916
Like, you just say, "Hey, let's all meet
in this park, this day and do something."

1296
01:01:43.917 --> 01:01:45.791
As of yesterday, our whole team

1297
01:01:45.792 --> 01:01:48.082
that we have together
was kinda feeling like,

1298
01:01:48.083 --> 01:01:50.499
we needed to cancel the event.

1299
01:01:58.875 --> 01:02:02.666
Utah was just making it
too impossible to put it on.

1300
01:02:02.667 --> 01:02:04.749
<i>♪ If I was me ♪</i>

1301
01:02:04.750 --> 01:02:06.666
<i>♪ Weight on my back ♪</i>

1302
01:02:06.667 --> 01:02:10.749
<i>♪ Feeling the sun upon my eyes ♪</i>

1303
01:02:10.750 --> 01:02:12.833
<i>♪ Where would I turn? ♪</i>

1304
01:02:12.834 --> 01:02:14.666
<i>♪ What would I burn? ♪</i>

1305
01:02:14.667 --> 01:02:18.791
<i>♪ I am a pawn within your hand ♪</i>

1306
01:02:18.792 --> 01:02:21.500
<i>♪ So many voices ♪</i>

1307
01:02:39.417 --> 01:02:42.833
<i>♪ Carving my blood
into the stone ♪</i>

1308
01:02:42.834 --> 01:02:44.999
<i>♪ What do I do? ♪</i>

1309
01:02:45.000 --> 01:02:46.874
<i>♪ Where do I turn? ♪</i>

1310
01:02:46.875 --> 01:02:50.749
<i>♪ Even my screams
cease to be heard ♪</i>

1311
01:02:50.750 --> 01:02:51.958
Bye, everybody. Bye.

1312
01:02:51.959 --> 01:02:54.416
Thanks, everyone.
Bye. Okay.

1313
01:02:54.417 --> 01:02:55.791
All right.
Thank you.

1314
01:02:56.792 --> 01:02:58.999
<i>♪ To be alone ♪</i>

1315
01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:02.458
<i>♪ So many choices ♪</i>

1316
01:03:06.834 --> 01:03:09.791
I was on a, a phone call

1317
01:03:09.792 --> 01:03:12.541
with, um,
one of my fund-raisers,

1318
01:03:12.542 --> 01:03:14.833
just going over
a bunch of details,

1319
01:03:14.834 --> 01:03:17.583
and my phone, uh,
my phone kept ringing.

1320
01:03:18.458 --> 01:03:20.290
I looked down,
and it was my mom.

1321
01:03:20.291 --> 01:03:22.499
I was like, ah, Mom.

1322
01:03:22.500 --> 01:03:26.332
Then she called again,
and then she called a third time.

1323
01:03:26.333 --> 01:03:30.040
And at that point, I realized,
I need to talk to my mom.

1324
01:03:30.041 --> 01:03:31.999
And, uh...

1325
01:03:32.000 --> 01:03:33.624
So I just said, hey,
I need to end this call.

1326
01:03:33.625 --> 01:03:35.666
I need to call my mom.

1327
01:03:35.667 --> 01:03:38.083
And I called my mom, and, um...

1328
01:03:39.667 --> 01:03:42.082
she was hysterical.

1329
01:03:49.000 --> 01:03:50.874
She told me my brother, Landon,

1330
01:03:50.875 --> 01:03:52.999
had just hung himself...

1331
01:03:57.709 --> 01:04:00.791
...in Provo.

1332
01:04:05.417 --> 01:04:06.958
<i>♪ In praise of you ♪</i>

1333
01:04:06.959 --> 01:04:08.374
<i>♪ Our faith is strong ♪</i>

1334
01:04:08.375 --> 01:04:10.958
<i>♪ We'll raise our colors
high in the blue ♪</i>

1335
01:04:10.959 --> 01:04:13.749
<i>♪ And cheer our Cougars of BYU ♪</i>

1336
01:04:13.750 --> 01:04:15.708
<i>♪ Oh, rah, rah, rah-rah-rah ♪</i>

1337
01:04:15.709 --> 01:04:19.457
So Landon was
attending BYU, the...

1338
01:04:19.458 --> 01:04:21.332
IDS church's university.

1339
01:04:21.333 --> 01:04:24.874
He also had a, uh,
really cool girlfriend,

1340
01:04:24.875 --> 01:04:28.499
and he'd kinda
blossomed down there.

1341
01:04:28.500 --> 01:04:31.290
And then he and his girlfriend,
they had sex,

1342
01:04:31.291 --> 01:04:33.332
which is against the honor code.

1343
01:04:33.333 --> 01:04:35.958
Landon was honest
with the university

1344
01:04:35.959 --> 01:04:38.750
and explained what had
happened, and told them.

1345
01:04:40.000 --> 01:04:42.082
And they said...

1346
01:04:43.709 --> 01:04:46.624
...you're kicked out
for five years, and...

1347
01:04:46.625 --> 01:04:49.582
you can't associate
with any of your professors.

1348
01:04:49.583 --> 01:04:50.792
You're done.

1349
01:04:52.458 --> 01:04:55.582
It started to put him into a
downward spiral of depression

1350
01:04:55.583 --> 01:04:59.749
and emotional wound after emotional
wound, it was... it was hard for him.

1351
01:04:59.750 --> 01:05:02.749
Even though in the eyes of his,

1352
01:05:02.750 --> 01:05:04.999
his God, he was clean.

1353
01:05:05.000 --> 01:05:06.457
In the culture there, he wasn't.

1354
01:05:06.458 --> 01:05:08.124
He was just a sinner.

1355
01:05:08.125 --> 01:05:11.457
And, uh, that's how a lot of
people looked at him.

1356
01:05:11.458 --> 01:05:13.833
As less than.

1357
01:05:13.834 --> 01:05:16.249
He just felt worthless.

1358
01:05:19.959 --> 01:05:21.416
So it was really hard,
because...

1359
01:05:25.333 --> 01:05:26.999
...night after night,
day after day,

1360
01:05:27.000 --> 01:05:30.290
I'm spending all my time
trying to bring this...

1361
01:05:30.291 --> 01:05:31.999
trying to bring
this festival to life,

1362
01:05:32.000 --> 01:05:36.333
to save lives and to help
people not feel alone.

1363
01:05:49.458 --> 01:05:51.833
It breaks my heart knowing
that Landon got to a point

1364
01:05:51.834 --> 01:05:54.332
where he believed
that the only way his soul

1365
01:05:54.333 --> 01:05:57.249
could go on was for it
to leave his body.

1366
01:05:58.583 --> 01:06:01.332
And the harsh reality is that,

1367
01:06:01.333 --> 01:06:04.207
I mean, here in Utah,
the leading cause of death

1368
01:06:04.208 --> 01:06:06.791
for teenagers is suicide.

1369
01:06:09.959 --> 01:06:14.499
I think we all can agree that we
need to find a solution to this.

1370
01:06:14.500 --> 01:06:17.708
And it's gonna take every
single one of us in this room

1371
01:06:17.709 --> 01:06:19.500
to make a difference.

1372
01:06:21.000 --> 01:06:23.417
I believe, and I know, that...

1373
01:06:26.458 --> 01:06:28.249
Mormons are good people.

1374
01:06:28.250 --> 01:06:30.666
That...

1375
01:06:30.667 --> 01:06:32.791
we have sincere hearts.

1376
01:06:32.792 --> 01:06:34.792
That we're no, no less...

1377
01:06:36.250 --> 01:06:38.791
broken than any other society.

1378
01:06:38.792 --> 01:06:39.792
Um...

1379
01:06:41.375 --> 01:06:43.958
But the way that our culture
is failing right now

1380
01:06:43.959 --> 01:06:46.249
is in a very unique way,

1381
01:06:46.250 --> 01:06:48.582
and in a deadly way.

1382
01:06:51.500 --> 01:06:57.457
The shaming that happens in
this culture needs to end.

1383
01:06:57.458 --> 01:06:58.749
I believe in a higher power,

1384
01:06:58.750 --> 01:07:01.124
and I believe in
goodness and love,

1385
01:07:01.125 --> 01:07:03.082
and I know we can do this.

1386
01:07:03.083 --> 01:07:06.999
This isn't some
insurmountable task.

1387
01:07:07.000 --> 01:07:10.916
It's feasible
because I believe in us.

1388
01:07:17.000 --> 01:07:18.582
I had to respond to him,
and I said,

1389
01:07:18.583 --> 01:07:22.874
Lance, I'm so sorry that your
brother just committed suicide.

1390
01:07:22.875 --> 01:07:24.582
You don't have
to do this anymore.

1391
01:07:24.583 --> 01:07:27.124
You know? You don't have
to be on these calls. Please.

1392
01:07:27.125 --> 01:07:30.124
Like, go take off time
with your family.

1393
01:07:30.125 --> 01:07:32.709
Like, you could, like,
I'll do LoveLoud.

1394
01:07:34.667 --> 01:07:37.457
And he... he just refuses.

1395
01:07:37.458 --> 01:07:39.333
He texted me and he says,

1396
01:07:41.083 --> 01:07:43.958
"I'm gonna be with my family
for a few days,

1397
01:07:43.959 --> 01:07:47.541
"but will still be working on
everything and want you to know

1398
01:07:47.542 --> 01:07:48.916
"we will make it happen.

1399
01:07:48.917 --> 01:07:51.916
"No one deserves to feel the way
my mother does right now,

1400
01:07:51.917 --> 01:07:53.916
"and I'm going to work
my hardest to ensure

1401
01:07:53.917 --> 01:07:56.249
"that this suicide
epidemic ends, man.

1402
01:07:56.250 --> 01:07:58.332
"This is so wrong
and has to stop.

1403
01:07:58.333 --> 01:08:00.624
"I know you're stressing
about this festival,

1404
01:08:00.625 --> 01:08:03.290
"but I assure you,
we're going to pull this off.

1405
01:08:03.291 --> 01:08:05.249
"There are too many
things going right.

1406
01:08:05.250 --> 01:08:06.624
"LoveLoud is going to happen

1407
01:08:06.625 --> 01:08:09.249
and it's going to
change the world."

1408
01:08:09.250 --> 01:08:11.666
He just said,
we're going to do this, Dan.

1409
01:08:11.667 --> 01:08:13.582
We can do this.

1410
01:08:13.583 --> 01:08:15.958
I have an idea.
Let's do it grassroots.

1411
01:08:15.959 --> 01:08:18.457
We don't need to get
a bunch of money.

1412
01:08:18.458 --> 01:08:19.999
We don't need to dumb it down

1413
01:08:20.000 --> 01:08:23.457
or clean it up or make it
more vanilla to get sponsors.

1414
01:08:23.458 --> 01:08:24.999
You know, you told me
on the phone that

1415
01:08:25.000 --> 01:08:26.332
if we didn't get the money,

1416
01:08:26.333 --> 01:08:29.499
we'd go stand in a park on...

1417
01:08:29.500 --> 01:08:33.332
...on a soapbox,
and just scream to the world

1418
01:08:33.333 --> 01:08:35.124
that things needed
to change in Utah.

1419
01:08:35.125 --> 01:08:39.082
We want it to be a safe space for
everybody to come out and be able to...

1420
01:08:39.083 --> 01:08:42.666
feel the love and acceptance
together for LGBTQ youth,

1421
01:08:42.667 --> 01:08:47.416
and we want them to hear it with
resounding cries from all across Utah.

1422
01:08:47.417 --> 01:08:50.290
We went from the
event not happening,

1423
01:08:50.291 --> 01:08:54.749
to me begging people
to take it on.

1424
01:08:54.750 --> 01:08:56.124
We have the chance
to do something

1425
01:08:56.125 --> 01:08:58.040
that's really
powerful and great,

1426
01:08:58.041 --> 01:08:59.416
but, um,

1427
01:08:59.417 --> 01:09:02.124
it has been, doing it
in Utah has been difficult.

1428
01:09:02.125 --> 01:09:05.374
Finally, we got somebody
who said okay, we can do it,

1429
01:09:05.375 --> 01:09:06.999
if we do it in this ballpark,

1430
01:09:07.000 --> 01:09:09.249
and we're gonna have
to set it up the morning of,

1431
01:09:09.250 --> 01:09:11.082
so we need a small stage
you can roll in.

1432
01:09:11.083 --> 01:09:13.999
A mutual love of music
is a great way to foster love,

1433
01:09:14.000 --> 01:09:16.999
understanding and acceptance.
That's how our next guest

1434
01:09:17.000 --> 01:09:20.165
wants to support
the LGBTQ community...

